    {
      "id": "s0j3f1u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Causes of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nq8rs7p",
      "content": "• Movement of tectonic plates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mnv7qjt",
      "content": "• Volcanic activity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ff8xp7p",
      "content": "• Faulting in Earth's crust."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vtrsn6w",
      "content": "• Human activities such as mining and dam construction."
    },
    {
      "id": "8k86vus",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Measurement of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "id": "fcoe061",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Scale</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Richter Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures magnitude (energy released).</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mercalli Scale</p>",
            "<p>Measures intensity based on damage observed.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "osos1l5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Effects of Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sfwea54",
      "content": "• Damage to buildings and infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o2q9vxk",
      "content": "• Landslides and ground cracks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kriv2ei",
      "content": "• Tsunamis in coastal regions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7dt4clg",
      "content": "• Loss of life and property."
    },
    {
      "id": "4co5k01",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Major Earthquake Zones of the World"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Focus vs. Epicenter: Focus is the subterranean source of seismic energy, while Epicenter is the surface point directly above the Focus.",
        "Wave Propagation: P-waves pass through solids, liquids, and gases; S-waves pass ONLY through solids.",
        "Richter vs. Mercalli: Richter measures magnitude (energy, quantitative 1-10), while Mercalli measures intensity (damage, qualitative I-XII)."
      ],
      "id": "q4ytsr4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hymwvgl",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jp02jxk",
      "content": "• Mid-Atlantic Ridge."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "go8wwia",
      "content": "• Himalayan belt."
    },
    {
      "id": "vvkx2jo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xdt27ky",
      "content": "• Pacific Ring of Fire has the highest number of volcanoes and earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tah3j3m",
      "content": "• P waves travel through solids and liquids; S waves travel only through solids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "we8j3co",
      "content": "• Epicenter is directly above the earthquake focus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wvf57pz",
      "content": "• Richter scale measures magnitude of earthquakes."
    }
  ],
